title: Settings › Sites and access › Read the roles and switch with View as
route: /settings
intro: A closed card on Settings that shows the rule the demo follows on every screen: access is by site (minimum necessary). A small table lists the four demo roles and the sites each can see, and 'View as' switches to a role, exactly as 'Viewing as' in the Demo menu does. It shows the rule; it is not an admin tool, so there is nothing to edit.
dir: TD
also: Demo only. The viewer is not saved between reloads. Settings itself is clinic-wide: the agents, their levels and Pause all are the same for every viewer.
---
start s1 "Open Settings\nThe card 'Sites and access' is the first card, closed\nSummary: 'Two sites, four roles'"
click cOpen "Click the card header, or Tab to it and press Enter or Space"
screen o1 "Card opens\nTwo short paragraphs, then a table: 'Person and role', 'Can see', 'Viewing as'"
process t1 "'Access is by site (minimum necessary). A person sees only the sites they work at, and every view and export respects it: lists, counts, charts, searches and downloads leave out the other site's patients.'"
process t2 "'A link to a record at a site someone cannot see opens a notice that names no patient. Agents, payers and these settings are clinic-wide. Roles are fixed in this demo, so use View as to see each one.'"

group gRows "The four rows"
  process r1 "Jordan Perez, UR coordinator\nSite A and Site B"
  process r2 "Alex Morgan, clinic owner\nSite A and Site B"
  process r3 "Dr. Rivera, Clinician, Site A\nSite A only"
  process r4 "Sam Okafor, Billing, Site B\nSite B only"
endgroup

process cur "The row of the current viewer shows a 'Viewing now' tag instead of a button"
click cView "Click 'View as' on another row, for example 'View as Dr. Rivera'"
store st "The viewer changes, and the site view becomes that person's sites\nSame as 'Viewing as' in the Demo menu"
toast tt "'Now viewing as Dr. Rivera'\n'Clinician, Site A. Only Site A is visible; the other site's records are not available.'"
process fl "The page itself does not change\nThe tag moves to Dr. Rivera's row\nThe top bar shows 'Site A only', the sidebar user card shows 'Dr. Rivera', badges recount"
click cClose "Click the header again"
process cl "Card closes"
endx nx "There is no edit control: no site picker per person, no add or remove a role, no Save"
goto g1 "Continues in: Global shell › Demo menu › Viewing as"
goto g2 "Continues in: Who can see what › Roles, sites and a record at the other site"
end e1 "Whoever is viewing now sees only their sites, on every screen"

s1 --> cOpen --> o1
o1 --> t1 & t2
o1 --> r1 & r2 & r3 & r4
r1 --> cur
r3 --> cView
cView --> st --> tt --> fl --> e1
o1 --> cClose --> cl
o1 -.-> nx
st -.-> g1
e1 --> g2
